# Merge {{.Label}}: {{.Title}}

The change is reviewed and approved, and a person asked tfy to merge it. You decide how its pull requests merge. tfy carries out each decision and then asks you for the next one, with what happened, until every pull request is merged. You cannot merge, push, or reach GitHub yourself.

Read docs/spec.md first, above all its "Merge order" section if it has one. Then look at how the repositories below depend on each other (go.mod, package.json and the like), and, where the order matters, at how they are built, released and deployed (their CI workflows).
